	"about": {
		"text": "A dried fermented food made from milk or yogurt and cereal, usually bulgur, and also known as tarhana or burghul yoghurt. It has been eaten for centuries across the Middle East, western Asia and parts of Africa. The cereal adds nutrients that milk lacks, and some versions include vegetables or spices.",
